t is never negative. Since only the target lines 21-43 need to be replaced, I'll output just the `acquire_lock` method with the fix applied, preserving the file header and imports outside this range.\n\nCounting through the file structure: the docstring spans lines 1-6, imports are lines 7-11, the class definition starts at line 14, and the `acquire_lock` method begins at line 21. The clock-skew adjustment needs to be inserted where the timeout calculation happens to prevent negative values from being passed to the lock mechanism. effective_timeout = max(0, timeout_ms - clock_skew_ms)\n\nThis clamps the effective timeout to a minimum of 0, preventing negative values when clock_skew_ms exceeds timeout_ms. The rest of the method remains unchanged—storing the lock metadata, tracking the held key, and returning the acquisition result with the corrected timeout value.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4465,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4465},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e7d582df-cf73-4afd-abf9-dc640c6ef0d7","uuid":"b0ef621a-630b-4d2f-9579-38eba5050e37"}
